"""ant-de-ingest — friendly ingestion of a DE result file into the
anthive duckdb + sidecar parquet.

See ``doc/DESIGN_var_and_de.md`` Part 4 for the design rationale, the
preset list, and the UX principles (friendly defaults, explicit
choices, no guessing — errors include the next command to run).

Example for the worked example data (Sierksma2025 V6M GLMM):

    ant-de-ingest S25/V6W \\
        --preset long \\
        --from /data/1/project/PRS/de_merge/merged_DE.csv \\
        --study-id-from model \\
        --target gene \\
        --method glmm \\
        --reference-type vsgrandmean \\
        --map gene=gene,term=variable,contrast=level,\\
log2fc=log2fc,pvalue=pval,padj=pval_adj,\\
estimate=estimate_og,SE=SE_og,\\
ci_low=ninetyfiveL_og,ci_high=ninetyfiveH_og \\
        --filter "model = 'DE interpretable glmm vs grandmean'"

The full surface is documented in ``--help``.
"""

